1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,280
Hello, West Bay Hotel. Can I help you?

2
00:00:02,280 --> 00:00:06,800
Oh, good morning. I'm ringing about your advertisement in the Evening Gazette.

3
00:00:06,800 --> 00:00:09,390
Is that the one for temporary staff?

4
00:00:09,390 --> 00:00:10,100
That's right.

5
00:00:10,100 --> 00:00:14,349
Yes. I'm afraid the person who's dealing with that isn't in today,

6
00:00:14,349 --> 00:00:17,890
but can give you the main details if you like.

7
00:00:17,890 --> 00:00:22,230
Yes please. Could you tell me what kind of staff you are looking for?

8
00:00:22,230 --> 00:00:24,750
We're looking for waiters at the moment.

9
00:00:24,750 --> 00:00:28,360
There was one post for a cook, but that's already been taken.

10
00:00:28,360 --> 00:00:31,940
Oh right. Erm, what are the hours of work?

11
00:00:31,940 --> 00:00:37,060
There are two different shifts - there's a day shift from 7 to 2

12
00:00:37,060 --> 00:00:40,260
and a late shift from 4 till 11.

13
00:00:40,260 --> 00:00:42,900
And can people choose which one they want to do?

14
00:00:42,900 --> 00:00:46,760
Not normally, because everyone would choose the day shift I suppose.

15
00:00:46,760 --> 00:00:49,170
You alternate from one week to another.

16
00:00:49,170 --> 00:00:53,770
Okay. I'm just writing all this down. What about time off?

17
00:00:53,770 --> 00:00:58,960
You get one day off and I think you can negotiate which one you want

18
00:00:59,260 --> 00:01:00,400
it's more or less up to you.

19
00:01:00,400 --> 00:01:02,800
But it has to be the same one every week.

20
00:01:02,800 --> 00:01:05,530
Do you know what the rates of pay are?

21
00:01:05,530 --> 00:01:13,420
Yes, I've got them here, You get £5.50 an hour, and that includes a break.

22
00:01:13,420 --> 00:01:15,570
Do I have to go home to eat or...

23
00:01:15,570 --> 00:01:19,540
You don't have to. You can get a meal in the hotel if you want to,

24
00:01:19,540 --> 00:01:22,270
and there's no charge for it, so you might as well.

25
00:01:22,270 --> 00:01:24,287
Oh good. Yes, so let's see.

26
00:01:24,287 --> 00:01:30,000
I'd get er, two hundred and twenty one, no, two hundred and thirty one pounds a week?

27
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:33,910
You'd also get tips - our guests tend to be quite generous.

28
00:01:33,910 --> 00:01:39,000
Erm, is there a uniform? What about clothes?

29
00:01:39,000 --> 00:01:41,200
Yes, I forgot to mention that

30
00:01:41,660 --> 00:01:45,560
You need to wear a white shirt, just a plain one, and dark trousers.

31
00:01:45,560 --> 00:01:49,730
You know, not green or anything like that. And we don't supply those.

32
00:01:49,730 --> 00:01:53,440
That's okay, I've got trousers, I'd just have to buy a couple of shirts.

33
00:01:53,440 --> 00:01:56,420
What about anything else? Do I need a waistcoat or anything?

34
00:01:56,420 --> 00:01:59,420
You have to wear a jacket, but the hotel lends you that.

35
00:01:59,420 --> 00:02:04,200
I see. Er, one last thing - I don't know what the starting date is.

36
00:02:04,200 --> 00:02:09,140
Just a minute, I think it's some time around the end of June

37
00:02:09,780 --> 00:02:12,400
Yes, the 28th, in time for the summer.

38
00:02:12,400 --> 00:02:14,800
That's great. I'm available from the 10th.

39
00:02:14,800 --> 00:02:19,900
Oh good. Well, if you can call again you need to speak to the Service Manager.

40
00:02:19,900 --> 00:02:28,120
Her name's Jane Urwin, that's U-R-W. I-N, and she'll probably arrange to meet you.

41
00:02:28,120 --> 00:02:31,150
Okay. And when's the best time to ring?

42
00:02:31,150 --> 00:02:35,775
Could you call tomorrow? Urn, she usually starts checking the rooms at midday,

43
00:02:35,775 --> 00:02:40,400
so before then if you can, so she'll have more time to chat.

44
00:02:40,400 --> 00:02:43,920
I'll just give you her number because she's got a direct line.

45
00:02:43,920 --> 00:02:44,560
Thanks.

46
00:02:44,560 --> 00:02:48,090
It's 832 double-0 9.

47
00:02:48,090 --> 00:02:51,000
823 double-0 9?

48
00:02:51,000 --> 00:02:53,200
832.

49
00:02:53,200 --> 00:02:55,730
Oh, okay. Yes, I'll do that.

50
00:02:55,730 --> 00:02:58,680
And by the way, she will ask you for a reference

51
00:02:59,040 --> 00:03:00,660
so you might like to be thinking about that.

52
00:03:00,660 --> 00:03:03,720
You know, just someone who knows you and can vouch for you.

53
00:03:03,720 --> 00:03:06,930
Yes, no problem. Well, thanks very much for your help.

54
00:03:06,930 --> 00:03:08,400
You're welcome. Bye.

55
00:03:08,400 --> 00:03:09,290
Bye.
